description:
Split from WT-19 (task-b1ca54f2716442be889a14623eb59983) DoD 5. The request is #architects msg-8285827e and the shape is architect-0fcb7226's msg-27859513. The human's go on the early worktree switch is #general msg-717a48e0.

Goal: before this project switches to worktree mode, prove three things on the post-WT-10M wrapper bytes:
- two parallel tasks and one conflict-resumed task land on main with fast-forward-only history;
- the control checkout follows;
- the candidate qualityGate passes in the sparse gate worktree.
If the run fails, the flip waits.

One new file: scripts/tests/worktree-e2e.cjs, modelled on postflight-worktree.cjs.
- It keeps WT-19 step 2's CLI: `<sh|ps1> <wrapper> <fake-proxy> <parent-tmp> <engine>`.
- It runs the real wrappers against the shared fake proxy, with no real daemon.
- Fixture under <parent-tmp>:
  - a `git init` repo whose first commit is this repo's HEAD tree, so the gate's scripts exist;
  - a local bare origin;
  - the control checkout on moe/control;
  - settings: worktreeMode 'on', consolidationBranch 'main', and qualityGate set to the candidate `bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh && npm run lint`.
- Scenarios: (a) parallel and (b) conflict-resume, as WT-19 step 2 defines them.

WT-19 step 2 already planned this file under the same name and CLI, and WT-19's step 6 gate line runs it. WT-19's re-check therefore runs it unchanged.

Why WT-10M alone is enough as a dependency: its chain is WT-10M → WT-13 → WT-12 → WT-11 → WT-10, so the LANDING-CONFLICT resume (WT-11) and the control follow (WT-13) are on HEAD before this row can be claimed. postflight-fake-proxy.js and postflight-worktree.cjs are lane files, so this row edits no existing file.

NOT in scope:
- any edit to an existing file;
- this repo's main, moe/control, settings or GitHub origin;
- the ps1 engine leg and scenario (c), the remote race. Both stay with WT-19.

Verification: `node scripts/tests/worktree-e2e.cjs sh scripts/moe-agent.sh scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js "$(mktemp -d -p /mnt/d/moe-scratch wt-e2e.XXXXXX)" "$(command -v bash)"`. Widen MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC if drvfs is slow.
